To me, saying someone is "playing Nethack the easy way" is a
paradoxical statement. IMHO The only "easy" way to play Nethack is to
cheat or to go into Explore or Wizard mode.

Nethack is one of the most difficult games to play, period. It strikes
me there are a *few* people out there (and I do not mean you, because
I have no idea who you are) who have played the game SO much and have
practically memorized the entire source code that they forget what it
was like to play Nethack their first million times or so. (I think I'm
only on my 788,422th attempt or so and don't know the source code at
all, so I have yet to achieve that viewpoint)

Moreover, Nethack is largely a game of patience--how many YASDs occur
because someone was going through messages too quickly, not paying
attention to hit points, forgetting they took their gloves off, etc.
etc.? Nethack is also a LONG game, and much longer than it used to be
several years ago (with added Sokoban, etc.) which increases the
temptation to go too fast.

Following that train of thought, getting a high score--i.e. being high
level--means that you probably played the game a good damn long time,
and deserve kudos for not letting your level get to your head and
retain the patience needed to make it to the end of the game alive.

Not to mention the fact that a higher XL means higher XL of monsters.
IIRC, when you're on your ascension run, monster difficulty is always
determined by XL, not DL. The game remains incrementally harder.

> A ludicrously high score says "I am a sad
> extinctionist".  A very low score says either "I am insanely good" or "I
> play silly tricks at the end of things".

Or it means--and MIND YOU this is entirely meant in good humor--"I
finally won as a 3rd level naked polyless Healer, but I have lost my
job, family, and friends to Nethack."

But the truth is--Nethack is supposed to be FUN. If it's more fun to
get a high score and see your name on the top of the list, that's
cool. If it's more fun to take on the extra challenges to get the oohs
and aahs from your friends, so be it. Or either, for your own
self-satisfaction. It is, regardless of how much time you put into it,
just a game. Enjoy it.

